## Performance checklist

- Filter/project before wide operations and broadcast only genuinely small inputs.
- Understand shuffle boundaries (`join`, `groupBy`, `distinct`, repartition).
- Prefer built-in expressions over Python UDFs; inspect `df.explain("formatted")`.
- Partition output by common, low/medium-cardinality predicates—not IDs.
- Treat skew explicitly (AQE, salting, pre-aggregation), and avoid tiny files.
